WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.844 --> 00:00:05.424
In this video you'll invite a teacher to your school. It takes about a minute.

2
00:00:05.925 --> 00:00:10.205
Open Invitations from the menu, and select Invite Teacher.

3
00:00:10.707 --> 00:00:18.097
Enter the teacher's email address, first name, and last name. Those three are required for every invitation.

4
00:00:18.598 --> 00:00:33.078
Choose the grade levels this teacher will teach: E-S for elementary, M-S for middle school, H-S for high school, or H-E for higher education. You can pick more than one, and at least one is required.

5
00:00:33.579 --> 00:00:41.689
You can also add a department, a role title, and a subject area. They're optional, but they make your lists easier to read later.

6
00:00:42.191 --> 00:00:52.531
If the email already belongs to someone with a Fixer Nation account, you'll see a note about it. That's fine. They'll be able to accept your invitation with their existing account.

7
00:00:53.033 --> 00:01:00.473
The personal message is a nice touch. A line like, welcome to the team, shows up in the email the teacher receives.

8
00:01:00.974 --> 00:01:09.914
Select Send Invitation. The teacher gets an email that says they're invited to join your school. The invitation is open for fourteen days.

9
00:01:10.416 --> 00:01:16.856
A seat is held for the teacher the moment you send it, so pending invitations count toward your seat total.

10
00:01:17.356 --> 00:01:30.846
Your new invitation appears in the list with the status Pending. When the teacher opens the email, it changes to Opened. When they create their account, it changes to Registered, and you'll get an email letting you know they've joined.

11
00:01:31.347 --> 00:01:36.777
If you have a whole staff to invite, the next video shows how to do it with a spreadsheet.
